{{!-- Security (TLS) card shared by the SMTP and IMAP proxy config pages.
      The checkbox decides whether this listener speaks TLS; which certificate
      it serves is decided on /admin/config/tls and only summarized here.

      It used to do both. Ticking it fired an ACME order in the foreground,
      before the setting had been saved, and unticked itself when the order
      failed - so the page stopped matching the stored setting, and the reason
      was never shown. The listener now always has a certificate to start with
      (a self-signed one if nothing better exists), which is what lets this be
      an ordinary checkbox again.
      Params:
        field - the TLS-enabled setting name, also the checkbox id/name
                (smtpServerTLSEnabled / imapProxyServerTLSEnabled) --}}
<div class="card bg-base-100 shadow-md mb-6">
    <div class="card-header">
        <h6 class="card-title text-primary">Security (TLS)</h6>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <div>
            {{> ui/setting-ref name=field}}

            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                {{> ui/checkbox id=field name=field label="Enable TLS Encryption" class="trigger-example-render"
                checked=(lookup values field) error=(lookup errors field)}}

                {{!-- shrink-0: the checkbox beside it is w-full, so without this the badge is the
                      flex item that gives way - it was squeezed to half its text and printed its
                      second line over the setting reference --}}
                {{#if tlsSummary.label}}
                {{#> ui/tooltip text=tlsSummary.label.title class="shrink-0"}}
                {{> ui/badge label=tlsSummary.label.text variant=tlsSummary.label.type elId="tls-label"}}
                {{/ui/tooltip}}
                {{/if}}
            </div>

            <span class="helper-text">
                {{#if tlsSummary.hostname}}
                Clients connect to <em>{{tlsSummary.hostname}}</em>, which is served with
                {{#if tlsSummary.certificate}}a {{tlsSummary.certificate.sourceLabel}} certificate{{else}}no
                certificate yet{{/if}}. Manage certificates on the <a href="/admin/config/tls"
                    class="link link-animated">TLS Certificates</a> page.
                {{else}}
                No hostname is configured, so this listener serves a self-signed certificate. Set a <a
                    href="/admin/config/service#settingsServiceUrl" class="link link-animated">Service URL</a> and
                manage certificates on the <a href="/admin/config/tls" class="link link-animated">TLS
                    Certificates</a> page.
                {{/if}}
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
